   "color": "2",
   "text": "### Question<br><br>Does the chemical-imbalance framing help understanding, or misstate the science?"
  },
  {
   "id": "deciding",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 460,
   "y": 120,
   "width": 400,
   "height": 170,
   "color": "6",
   "text": "### Evidence that would decide<br><br>Studies of how people understand explanations, and whether explanation quality changes engagement or self-blame; replications of transmitter-level findings with medication status controlled."
  },
  {
   "id": "guard",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 920,
   "y": 120,
   "width": 340,
   "height": 170,
   "color": "2",
   "text": "### Overreach guard<br><br>Do not treat a communication hypothesis as evidence about mechanism, or the reverse."
  },
  {
   "id": "legend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 0,
   "y": -60,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 160,
   "color": "5",
   "text": "### Legend<br><br>Green: support for the framing.<br>Orange: tension or counter-evidence.<br>Purple: deciding evidence and hypotheses.<br>Edges label the relationship, not proof."
